# PHPStan baseline — BE-F11, generated 2026-09-16 at 585 findings (490 entries) with
# the configuration in phpstan.neon and no code touched. Paid down to 479 findings
# (384 entries) when BelongsToChannel::scopeAcrossChannels gained Builder<static>
# generics, and to 475 (380 entries) when the rep tests were cleared (2026-09-18).
# No identifier is ignored: the
# 213 relation declarations without a related type (`missingType.generics`) are counted
# here beside the 173 "undefined property on Model" symptoms they cause, so fixing a
# declaration takes its symptoms with it and the number only ever falls.
#
# This file is the debt, counted. It is not a place to add to. The rules:
#   - The total (the sum of every `count:` below) only falls. It is pinned exactly by
#     tests/Architecture/PhpstanBaselineTest.php, which fails the build when the sum rises
#     and asks for the pin to be lowered when it falls — so the number is always known,
#     never discovered.
#   - It is paid down one module at a time, each as its own small ticket under BE-F11
#     (the per-module table there is the work list, ranked by symptoms per declaration):
#     fix the module's declarations, regenerate this file, lower the pin, commit the three
#     together.
#   - A new finding in new code is not baselined; it is fixed. `--generate-baseline` is
#     run only in a pay-down commit, where the sum goes down.
#   - Nothing here is a runtime defect as of the date above: declarations without their
#     generic type, the bare-Model symptoms of those, arrays without a value type,
#     unresolved templates, and 31 Pest residues the analyser cannot express.
